he time to break even\n3. **Raise (640+):** Would be a risky bluff with just one pair, likely gets called by better hands\n\nReason:\nWhile I have pot odds of 2.25:1 requiring only ~31% equity to call, the opponent's river raise after passive play is very suspicious. With only a pair of Queens and a weak kicker (5), I'm likely behind against most hands that would raise the river here. The straight possibility (K-9), better Queens, two pairs, and sets are all very real threats. Given that I'm already down 450 chips cumulatively and need to manage my stack wisely for the remaining 12 hands, I should avoid marginal situations where I'm likely behind. The river raise represents strength, and my hand is just a mediocre pair.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
